WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.934
-Yeah. Oh, look at that.

00:00:01.934 --> 00:00:05.337
-Hello. How are you?
You didn't get the memo.

00:00:05.337 --> 00:00:08.007
-[ Laughs ] I should have.

00:00:08.007 --> 00:00:10.743
-So I'm just --
How much of a fool do I look?

00:00:10.743 --> 00:00:13.412
-No, you -- I can't believe --

00:00:13.412 --> 00:00:15.582
Of course you would do this.
You're the best.

00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:18.317
-This is how I walk around
my house all the time.

00:00:18.317 --> 00:00:20.052
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:00:20.052 --> 00:00:22.354
-I insist everybody who comes
to the door has to put one on.

00:00:22.354 --> 00:00:24.257
And know how to tie it --
that's the other thing.

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:26.859
-Yeah. So it's classy,
but it's also dressed down.

00:00:26.859 --> 00:00:29.528
It's both.
You know how to do it.

00:00:29.528 --> 00:00:31.797
Today is James Bond Day.
-That's right.

00:00:31.797 --> 00:00:33.366
-There's no better way
to celebrate

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:35.200
than with James Bond himself.
I'm honored.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:37.737
Thank you so much for coming.
-Pleasure is all mine.

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:39.705
-Oh, please.
-Thank you for having me.

00:00:39.705 --> 00:00:43.176
-It was announced on Friday that
the release of "No Time to Die"

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:45.744
is now being pushed
till the spring.

00:00:45.744 --> 00:00:48.615
And I have a question for you.
Be honest.

00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:50.750
Is this just because
you want to be James Bond

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:52.518
for a few months longer?

00:00:52.518 --> 00:00:55.255
-Just eke every second I can
out of it.

00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:57.256
-Yeah.
-Here's the deal.

00:00:57.256 --> 00:00:59.058
This thing is just
bigger than all of us,

00:00:59.058 --> 00:01:02.562
and we just want people
to go and see this movie

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:04.964
in the right way and safe way.

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:09.735
You know, cinemas, you know,
all around the world

00:01:09.735 --> 00:01:12.071
are closed at the moment,
and we want to release the movie

00:01:12.071 --> 00:01:14.908
at the same time
all around the world,

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:18.010
and this isn't the right time.
-Yeah.

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:20.213
-So, you know, fingers crossed,

00:01:20.213 --> 00:01:22.381
April 2nd
is going to be our date.

00:01:22.381 --> 00:01:24.717
-It's such a big film.
-Yes.

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:27.320
-And all of these Bonds are,

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:31.457
but they have been ever since
you took over 15 years ago.

00:01:31.457 --> 00:01:33.492
They're just the most insane --

00:01:33.492 --> 00:01:36.829
Every movie would top each other
with the next one.

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:38.798
And I'm just like --
You know, some people go like,

00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:41.000
"Oh, my gosh, why wouldn't you
just want that gig forever?"

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.402
I'm like, "Because
it's hard work. It's crazy."

00:01:43.402 --> 00:01:45.404
-You know, I mean, there
comes a time where, you know --

00:01:45.404 --> 00:01:48.507
I've given it everything I can.

00:01:48.507 --> 00:01:51.710
I'm so glad that I came back
and did this last one.

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:54.780
We had lots of loose threads
that we hadn't tied up,

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:58.417
and the story,
it just didn't feel complete.

00:01:58.417 --> 00:02:00.453
And I just was so --

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:03.822
You know, I needed a break,
I'll truly admit it.

00:02:03.822 --> 00:02:06.725
I just needed to kind of get my
head away from it for a while,

00:02:06.725 --> 00:02:09.962
and once I had and we started
talking about story lines

00:02:09.962 --> 00:02:12.632
and things that we could do
and where we could take it,

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:14.867
I was like, "Oh, look, I'm in.
Let's do one more

00:02:14.867 --> 00:02:17.102
and try to sort of, like,
finish the story."

00:02:17.102 --> 00:02:19.505
We started the story
in "Casino Royale,"

00:02:19.505 --> 00:02:21.807
and actually we've
kind of been very -- You know.

00:02:21.807 --> 00:02:23.976
I think we very successfully
kind of continued that story

00:02:23.976 --> 00:02:25.477
all the way through.

00:02:25.477 --> 00:02:27.813
And this was the chance
to just round it off.

00:02:27.813 --> 00:02:30.082
-Do you remember
when it was formally announced?

00:02:30.082 --> 00:02:33.386
You can take it off. Sure, sure.
Take it off. Yeah.

00:02:33.386 --> 00:02:35.888
Do you remember
when you were formally announced

00:02:35.888 --> 00:02:38.157
as the next James Bond,
when it was official?

00:02:38.157 --> 00:02:41.293
-Yeah, I mean, I will never
forget any of that time.

00:02:41.293 --> 00:02:43.930
It was some of the most
exciting, dramatic --

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:46.199
all of the things --
time of my life.

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:49.569
I was in -- God.

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:52.070
When it was
officially announced --

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:54.207
That's just now I think
it was officially announced,

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:56.442
like, 15 years ago, like this
week or something, or next week.

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:59.746
-Yeah, it is. Yeah.
-But I was in Baltimore

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:02.147
filming with Nicole Kidman.

00:03:02.147 --> 00:03:05.317
And Barbara Broccoli,

00:03:05.317 --> 00:03:07.486
the producer of the Bonds,

00:03:07.486 --> 00:03:09.956
one of the producers
of the Bonds,

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:14.326
phoned me up and just said
to me, "Over to you, kiddo."

00:03:14.326 --> 00:03:16.395
-Oh!

00:03:16.395 --> 00:03:17.830
-But this is the thing.

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:20.232
You know, I was in Baltimore.
I had a night off.

00:03:20.232 --> 00:03:22.868
I had a day off the following
day, and I was like,

00:03:22.868 --> 00:03:24.870
"Well, what am I going to do?
I can't tell anybody."

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:26.706
I couldn't tell anybody
because it was like --

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:28.274
She said, "Don't tell a soul.

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:29.975
Don't tell your family.
Don't tell."

00:03:29.975 --> 00:03:31.945
So I'm like...like --

00:03:31.945 --> 00:03:34.847
So, I was in
Whole Foods supermarket

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:37.416
literally with a shopping cart

00:03:37.416 --> 00:03:40.486
with deodorant
and washing liquid

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:42.655
and, you know,
doing my weekly shopping.

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:44.557
So, I literally pushed that

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:47.260
like, you know,
down an aisle like that,

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:50.462
and walked into
the liquor section.

00:03:50.462 --> 00:03:52.998
I bought myself a bottle of
vodka, a bottle of vermouth,

00:03:52.998 --> 00:03:55.001
and a shaker and a glass.

00:03:55.001 --> 00:03:57.103
And I went back.

00:03:57.103 --> 00:04:00.039
And this is the thing.
You may not believe this.

00:04:00.039 --> 00:04:01.941
I'd never had a martini before.

00:04:01.941 --> 00:04:04.176
I'd never mixed myself
a martini, ever.

00:04:04.176 --> 00:04:06.245
I'd never actually drunk
a martini before.

00:04:06.245 --> 00:04:07.613
I kind of understood
what it was,

00:04:07.613 --> 00:04:09.582
and I was like, "Okay.
I'm going to give this a go."

00:04:09.582 --> 00:04:11.484
People talk about --
It was in Chicago I think

00:04:11.484 --> 00:04:13.052
when I was doing
"Road to Perdition"

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:14.654
when people were drinking
martinis --

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:16.455
the first time I'd ever seen
a proper martini.

00:04:16.455 --> 00:04:18.224
And I did actually taste one.

00:04:18.224 --> 00:04:19.692
Then I went,
"This is just vodka."

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:21.994
And they went, "Yeah."
I said, "Very dry."

00:04:21.994 --> 00:04:24.297
[ Speaking indistinctly ]

00:04:24.297 --> 00:04:26.899
-Yeah, it's so dry
that it's just actually vodka.

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:29.268
-It's just a glassful of vodka!
Let's be honest.

00:04:29.268 --> 00:04:33.673
So I did half a bottle and
stumbled to a bar in Baltimore,

00:04:33.673 --> 00:04:35.975
of which there are many really
many good bars in Baltimore.

00:04:35.975 --> 00:04:37.710
-Yeah, I love Baltimore.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.278
-If you put a gun
against my head,

00:04:39.278 --> 00:04:42.048
I couldn't find the bar again,
I was so drunk when I got there.

00:04:42.048 --> 00:04:44.617
And I sat and I must have drunk
another three martinis

00:04:44.617 --> 00:04:46.318
at the bar. And the guy --
I must have been smiling.

00:04:46.318 --> 00:04:48.921
I just must have been, like,
from ear to ear.

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:50.790
And the guy kept on saying,
"What's going on?

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:52.491
What's going on?
You're in a good mood."

00:04:52.491 --> 00:04:54.860
I said, "Listen,
you wouldn't [bleep]

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:56.929
believe me if I told you."

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:58.564
-He's like,
"This guy's crazy, man.

00:04:58.564 --> 00:05:01.934
What is -- He's just laughing
going, 'I'm James Bond!'"

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:05.337
-I must have literally --
I must have been...

00:05:05.337 --> 00:05:07.306
I can't imagine.
I must have looked crazy.

00:05:07.306 --> 00:05:10.943
I mean, the fact he even spoke
to me was probably, you know --

00:05:10.943 --> 00:05:12.745
-But what a tough thing
to keep secret.

00:05:12.745 --> 00:05:14.347
And you're just like,
"Oh, my gosh."

00:05:14.347 --> 00:05:17.216
But, I mean, there is one person
you did tell,

00:05:17.216 --> 00:05:18.918
which I love this story.

00:05:18.918 --> 00:05:20.953
You told your mom.

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:24.690
-Yeah, of course.
I mean, you know, I did.

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:27.059
And then she got --
Yeah, that's right. Yeah.

00:05:27.059 --> 00:05:32.198
I told my mother, and she
then got done by the press.

00:05:32.198 --> 00:05:34.066
Because she is
very tight-lipped.

00:05:34.066 --> 00:05:37.703
But, of course, she got a phone
call from "The London Times,"

00:05:37.703 --> 00:05:41.040
who basically said,
"You must be very proud."

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:43.075
And she was like,
"Well, of course I'm proud."

00:05:43.075 --> 00:05:44.977
And then that's it.
-That's all they needed.

00:05:44.977 --> 00:05:47.747
-Daniel Craig's mum
announces Bond.

00:05:47.747 --> 00:05:49.648
-Confirms it.
-Which is not actually,

00:05:49.648 --> 00:05:51.583
when you think about it,
not a bad way to get announced.

00:05:51.583 --> 00:05:54.153
Is it, really?
-Everyone is going to be

00:05:54.153 --> 00:05:56.455
asking you about what you will
miss most about being Bond.

00:05:56.455 --> 00:05:58.157
I was going to ask you,
what's the one thing

00:05:58.157 --> 00:06:01.961
that you won't miss at all
about being James Bond?

00:06:01.961 --> 00:06:05.030
-Um, I don't get out very often,

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:07.934
but sometimes
I will be somewhere,

00:06:07.934 --> 00:06:10.303
maybe in a hotel lobby
or somewhere,

00:06:10.303 --> 00:06:12.771
you know,
where there's a bar maybe.

00:06:12.771 --> 00:06:15.407
It can be literally 9:00 a.m.
in the morning.

00:06:15.407 --> 00:06:18.410
And a martini will be shoved
in front of me.

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:19.679
And I'm like --

00:06:19.679 --> 00:06:21.680
Back in the day,
there may be a time

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:24.216
when a 9:00 a.m. martini may
have been a kind of nice thing.

00:06:24.216 --> 00:06:26.518
But just -- I'm just not.
They don't go down so well now.

00:06:26.518 --> 00:06:27.953
9:00 a.m.?

00:06:27.953 --> 00:06:29.789
I love a Martini,
but 9:00 a.m. is a bit tough.

00:06:29.789 --> 00:06:31.390
I won't miss that.

00:06:31.390 --> 00:06:33.492
-We have an exclusive clip
from "No Time to Die"

00:06:33.492 --> 00:06:36.028
that we're premiering right here
when we come back.

00:06:36.028 --> 00:06:37.763
I've actually
never even seen it yet.

00:06:37.763 --> 00:06:39.665
It's a special link.
So I'm freaking out.

00:06:39.665 --> 00:06:42.068
Thanks for this.
Stick around, everybody.

